    "summary": "Built the pure \u00a75 claim rules. packages/content/src/claim: claimRules (channelTicks 200 = 10 s x 20, deadlineTicks 42000 = 35 min, circleRadiusTiles 4) with a zod validator (channel 0 allowed as instant victory). packages/simulation/src/claim: createClaimConfig/createClaimState, stepClaim(config, state, tickInput) -> {state, events} in a fixed phase order (reservations, active channel break/advance, start by closest-then-lowest-id, completion, deadline), replayClaim, and the events claim-interrupted/protection-ended/claim-started/claim-completed/duel-ended-without-theft/match-ended. It never mutates its input and freezes after a result. Added one subpath export each (@pirate-sea-race/simulation/claim, @pirate-sea-race/content/claim) and docs/claim.md. Tests: scripted rule tests with deep-frozen inputs, 60 seeded random scripts (at most one winner, frozen after the result, per-tick invariants, replay hashes, every interrupt reason covered), and symmetry tests (input reordering, rotations and mirrors, order-preserving relabelling, a 1000-trial oracle under random relabelling). Executed from this worktree after npm ci: npm run typecheck (exit 0), npm run test:unit (425/425 pass), npm run test:integration (22/22 pass), npm run build (exit 0, smoke passed). Also confirmed by hand that both claim subpaths load from dist/, and that the purity test flags a Math.random planted in each new directory (then removed).",
